+## Approach
+
+Recursive diff using the existing `jsonEqual`, `parsePointer`-compatible pointer escaping (`~`→`~0`, `/`→`~1`) and `clone`.
+
+- Equal values: no operations.
+- Both objects: for keys removed emit `remove`; for keys added emit `add`; for common keys recurse.
+- Both arrays: trim common prefix and suffix, then recurse pairwise over the overlapping part of the remaining middle, then `remove` surplus old elements (all at the same index) or `add` surplus new ones (ascending indices). Operations are emitted in an order that is valid when applied sequentially.
+- Otherwise (differing types or scalars): `replace` at the path (root path `""`).
+
+Added/replaced values are cloned so the patch shares no structure with `to`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- No `move`/`copy` detection: keeps output simple and always correct; arrays use prefix/suffix trimming rather than full LCS.
+- Members whose value is `undefined` are not JSON and are not considered.
