+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document rather than the whole new version. `applyPatch` exists but nothing produces a patch.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to`.
+- The diff is recursive (objects by member, arrays by element) so a small change yields a small patch, never a whole-document replacement unless the root types differ.
+- Inputs are never mutated; the patch shares no structure with them.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: adds patch generation alongside patch application.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new exported function; README and tests updated. No breaking changes.
